article-title>Elevated Human Telomerase Reverse Transcriptase Gene Expression in Blood Cells Associated with Chronic Arsenic Exposure in Inner Mongolia, China</article-title><source>Environ Health Perspect</source><year>2009</year><comment>In press</comment></citation></ref><ref id="b13-ijerph-06-01010"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mo</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Xia</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Wade</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmitt</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Le</surname><given-names>XC</given-names></name><name><surname>Dang</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Mumford</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chronic arsenic exposure and oxidative stress: OGG1 expression and arsenic exposure, nail selenium, and skin hyperkeratosis in inner mongolia</article-title><source>Environ. Health Perspect</source><year>2006</year><volume>114</volume><fpage>835</fpage><lpage>841</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16759981</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14-ijerph-06-01010"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gong</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Lu</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Watta</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Wena</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Hea</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Mumford</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Ning</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Xia</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Le</surname><given-names>XC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Speciation analysis of arsenic in groundwater from Inner Mon